remstart
    THE ANGLER
    an old angler fish who lives in the dark, and knows how the sea works. the "bright idea" card
    brings it, and it answers a question. the routines are in fish_routines_angler, and the tests
    are in fish_tests_angler. the pictures are drawn by Tools/angler_art_gen.py.

    THE CARD. "bright idea" is an instant, and it is dealt like any other card, by the seed. it is
    rare: when the deal lands on it, one more roll of the cards says if it stays (ANGLER_DEAL_CHANCE).
    that roll is on the stream of the cards, so a seed deals it the same way every time. nothing that
    the player knows has a say in whether it is dealt. it is not in the book, which has no room for
    it, and it is not written in the log of a game, which has no room for its number either.

    THE QUESTIONS. when the card is taken, the upgrade screen goes away, the dark of info mode comes
    down, and the angler swims in at the bottom of the screen with its light. it offers three
    questions, and a fourth line that keeps the light for later. which questions they are is picked
    with rnd, never with a stream: they depend on what this player has heard before, and a stream
    roll that one player makes and another does not would make the same seed deal two games.
        the first is about something that is on the board right now, if anything there has not been
        explained yet. a question asked from info mode puts the thing that was highlighted here.
        the second is about anything else that has not been explained yet.
        the third is a rumor: a secret of the sea. the rumors come in tiers, and a tier is only
        offered once every rumor of the tier before it has been heard. the last tier is silly, and
        only comes once all of the true ones have been heard. the rumors of the coral wait until
        coral has grown, in any game, so that the angler does not give the coral away. see
        anglerRumorOpen.
    once every plain question has been heard, the ones that were heard longest ago come around
    again. ANGLER_HEARD keeps when each topic was last heard, as a count that only goes up.
    the answer is one or two pages. while it is being said, the hole in the dark goes to the part
    of the screen that it is about, if it is about one, so the light of the angler shows it.

    KEEPING THE LIGHT. the fourth line keeps the question for later. it is kept in the preferences,
    so it lasts from one game to the next. there is room for ANGLER_BANK_MAX of them: with that many,
    the line is dim and cannot be picked. the card is still dealt then, because the seed deals it.
    a kept light is a little bulb, {bulb}, after the hint for info mode along the bottom of the
    screen, one for every light. in info mode the hint says that the confirm button asks, and asking
    spends one. the confirm button on a special move still opens the page that moves the moves.
    asking from info mode has a line that goes back without asking, in place of keeping the light.

    THE VOICE. the angler says its words one letter at a time, and talks in bubbles: every vowel that
    starts a run of vowels plays a little bubble for that vowel. there are six of them: ah, eh, ee,
    oh, oo and uh. Tools/angler_voice_gen.py makes them, in one of a few styles, and renders samples
    of every style saying whole lines, by the same rules as these:
        the last word before a question mark goes up, a little more for every bubble of it.
        a word before ! is louder.
        the last word before ... fades away, every bubble quieter than the one before.
        a comma, and the end of a sentence, are a pause.
    the confirm button says the rest of it at once. the engine draws only the letters that have
    been said, with `set text reveal`, and the line is laid out whole from the start, so the words do
    not jump from line to line as they come. anglerSpeakStep does it, on every frame of the scene.

    THE CALL. HELP, or INFO, tapped out on the radio, brings the angler too, without the card and
    without a light, as often as it is called. see MORSE in fish_headers. the two words share one entry
    in the codec, in the signals, right after the words that bring somebody swimming through, and right
    before the usual ending: CODEC_ENTRY_CALL. it waits for the radio to tap back its R, the way it does
    for any word, and comes a moment after that. it offers its questions, and a line that goes back without
    asking. after it has answered, it asks if there is anything else: another question, with new ones
    picked about the board as it is then, or goodbye for now. a deep rumor tells of the call.

    THE FIRST MEETING. the very first time that the player meets the angler, however that came about, it
    says who it is before it offers anything: that it is a friend, and that it can help. and when it
    has answered that first question, it says, before it goes, that its light can be kept for later,
    up to ANGLER_BANK_MAX of them, from game to game, and asked in info mode. when the light was kept
    the first time, that was said already, so it goes without it. ANGLER_MET says if it has happened,
    and it is kept in the preferences. "forget what was heard", in the debug window, forgets it too.

    every answer must be true, the rumors most of all. a player who is told a lie by the one who
    explains things stops listening. the silly ones say plainly that they are silly. TUNA is never
    told: it turns on the debug mode.
remend

` the card. an instant, so it is a constant, like the other instants: handle_ability_instant_effect picks between them by number.
#constant ABILITY_INDEX_ANGLER 35
global ANGLER_DEAL_CHANCE = 35 `how many times in a hundred the deal keeps it, when it lands on it

global ANGLER_BANK_MAX = 4 `how many lights can be kept for later
global ANGLER_BANKED = 0 `how many are kept. it is read from the preferences when the game starts.
global ANGLER_PENDING = 0 `1 when the card has been taken, and the angler comes once the upgrade screen has gone
global ANGLER_FROM_CARD = 0 `1 while the angler came for the card, and 0 while it came from info mode, or the radio
global ANGLER_FROM_RADIO = 0 `1 while it came because it was called on the radio. see THE CALL.
global ANGLER_CALL_PENDING = 0 `1 when it has been called. it comes once the radio has tapped back its answer.
global ANGLER_CALL_PAUSE_MS = 400 `how long after the answer it comes, in milliseconds
global ANGLER_CALL_AT_MS = 0 `when it comes, once the answer is over, or 0 while it is still being tapped
global MORSE_WORD_HELP = 15 `the two words that call it. they come after the words of the cameos.
global MORSE_WORD_INFO = 16
global CODEC_ENTRY_CALL = -1 `the entry that the two of them share, once setup_codec has run
global ANGLER_ANCHOR = -1 `the topic of the thing that was highlighted in info mode, or -1
global ANGLER_FOUND = -1 `what the last of the functions that look for a topic, or a blob, found
global dim ANGLER_CANDIDATES(64) `the topics that one of those is picking between

` what is on the board, when the angler comes. see anglerScanBoard.
global ANGLER_SEE_STACK = 0
global ANGLER_SEE_BELLY = 0
global ANGLER_SEE_BONES = 0
global ANGLER_SEE_JELLY = 0
global ANGLER_SEE_RAY = 0
global ANGLER_SEE_BOTTLE = 0

` where it is all kept, in the preferences. it must not move.
global ANGLER_PREF = 4000 `the lights that are kept, then the count of what has been heard, then whether it has been met
global ANGLER_PREF_HEARD = 4100 `and when each topic was heard, one number for each

` THE TOPICS. every one is a number, in the order that they are made in setup_angler_topics. the
` numbers are kept in the preferences, so a new topic goes on the end.
#constant ANGLER_TIER_PLAIN 0
#constant ANGLER_TIER_RUMOR 1
#constant ANGLER_TIER_DEEP 2
#constant ANGLER_TIER_SILLY 3
global ANGLER_TOPIC_ROOM = 64
global ANGLER_TOPIC_COUNT = 0
global dim ANGLER_ASK$(64) `the question, as the player would ask it. these three are keys of angler.csv.
global dim ANGLER_SAY$(64) `the answer
global dim ANGLER_MORE$(64) `and the second page of it, when there is one, or " "
global dim ANGLER_PAGES(64) `1 or 2
global dim ANGLER_TIER(64)
global dim ANGLER_HEARD(64) `when it was last heard, or 0 for never. see ANGLER_STAMP.
global ANGLER_STAMP = 0 `goes up by one for every answer
global ANGLER_MET = 0 `1 once the player has met the angler, in any game. see THE FIRST MEETING.

` the questions that are on offer, and the line under them
global dim ANGLER_PICK(3)
global ANGLER_PICK_COUNT = 0
global ANGLER_CHOICE = 0 `the line that is highlighted. ANGLER_PICK_COUNT is the line under the questions.
global ANGLER_LINE_LAST = 0 `the last of the lines that are up: the line under the questions, or the second of the two that ask if there is anything else
global ANGLER_ASKED = -1 `the topic that was picked, or -1 when the light was kept, or nothing was asked

` THE SCENE
global ANGLER_SCALE = 2 `how many pixels of the game a pixel of the pictures is
global ANGLER_TIP_X = 47 `where the light hangs from, in the pixels of Angler.png. see ANGLER_TIP in Tools/angler_art_gen.py.
global ANGLER_TIP_Y = 9
global ANGLER_ART_W = 52 `how big Angler.png is, in its own pixels
global ANGLER_ART_H = 34
global ANGLER_GLOW_DROP = 12 `how far below the tip the middle of the glow is, in pixels of the game: the bulb hangs down
global ANGLER_GLOW_R = 255 `the color of the glow around its light
global ANGLER_GLOW_G = 220
global ANGLER_GLOW_B = 140
global ANGLER_OWN_BULB = 0 `1 when the light is drawn into the picture, so the bulb that hangs from the tip is not shown
global ANGLER_SHIFT_X = 0 `how far right of where the old picture was the picture is, so that a smaller one still sits by the box
global TEX_ANGLER_HAPPY = 0 `the picture of it while it talks, or 0 for the same picture all the time

` THE NEW ART'S ANGLER. with the new art (see THE NEW ART in fish_headers_customart), the angler is the one
` that was drawn for it: 32 pixels, facing left, so it is turned around to face the box it swims up to.
` its light is drawn into the picture, at ANGLER_TIP_X, ANGLER_TIP_Y once it is turned around, so the
` bulb of the old one is not shown, and the glow is in the teal of that light. it has a happy face, for
` while it is talking. its outline is the deep-water blue of the line around the fish on the board.
` setup_angler puts all of that in place.
global ORDER_ANGLER_TEXT = ORDER_INFO_TEXT + 10 `the words. see setup_angler for why they are so far above the box.
global ANGLER_BOX_W = 404 `the box that it talks in
global ANGLER_BOX_H = 96
global ANGLER_LIGHT_HOLE = 70 `how big the hole in the dark is around the light, when it is not showing anything
global ANGLER_SWIM_MS = 700 `how long it takes to swim in, and out
global ANGLER_SPRITE = 0
global ANGLER_BULB_SPRITE = 0
global ANGLER_GLOW_SPRITE = 0
global ANGLER_BOX_SPRITE = 0
global ANGLER_BOX_BORDER as infoBorder
global ANGLER_CURSOR as infoBorder
global ANGLER_SAY_TEXT_ID = 0
global dim ANGLER_LINE_TEXTS(4) `the questions, and the line under them
global ANGLER_SWIM_TWEEN_ID = 0 `0 when it is off the screen to the left, and 1 when it is where it talks from
global ANGLER_UP_TWEEN_ID = 0 `0 when it talks from the bottom of the screen, and 1 from the top
global ANGLER_SAY_FADE_TWEEN_ID = 0 `the words fade in
global ANGLER_LINES_SHOWN = 0 `1 while the questions are showing
global ANGLER_SPOT = -1 `the info blob that the light is showing, or -1 for the light itself
global ANGLER_SPOT_X = 0 `and where it is. see anglerSpotRect.
global ANGLER_SPOT_Y = 0
global ANGLER_SPOT_W = 0
global ANGLER_SPOT_H = 0
global ANGLER_HOLE_X# = 0 `where the hole in the dark is now. it slides to where it should be.
global ANGLER_HOLE_Y# = 0
global ANGLER_HOLE_W# = 0
global ANGLER_HOLE_H# = 0
global ANGLER_FRAME_DONE = 0 `1 once frame_angler has laid everything out at least once

` THE VOICE
global ANGLER_LETTER_MS = 38 `how long a letter takes to say
global ANGLER_COMMA_MS = 150 `and a comma, or a colon
global ANGLER_STOP_MS = 260 `and the end of a sentence
global ANGLER_VOICE_VOLUME# = .55 `the same as VOICE_VOLUME in Tools/angler_voice_gen.py
global ANGLER_ASK_PITCH# = .35 `how much the last word before a ? goes up, in octaves
global ANGLER_ASK_STEP# = .12 `and how much more for every bubble of it after the first
global ANGLER_SHOUT# = 1.6 `how many times as loud a word is before a !
global ANGLER_TRAIL# = .55 `every bubble of the last word before ... is this many times as loud as the one before
global ANGLER_JITTER# = .06 `how far the pitch of a bubble wanders, either way, in octaves
global dim SFX_CLIP_ANGLER(6) `ah, eh, ee, oh, oo, uh
global ANGLER_VOICE_ROOM = 4 `how many bubbles can be sounding at once
global dim ANGLER_VOICE_SFX(4)
global ANGLER_VOICE_NEXT = 0
global ANGLER_SPEAKING = 0 `1 while a line is being said
global ANGLER_SAID = 0 `how many letters of it have been said
global ANGLER_SAY_NEXT_MS = 0 `when the next one is due
global ANGLER_WORD_BUBBLES = 0 `how many bubbles the word that is being said has had
global ANGLER_WORD_END = 0 `how the word that a letter is in ends: 0, or 1 for ?, 2 for !, and 3 for ...
global TEX_ANGLER
global TEX_ANGLER_BULB
global TEX_ANGLER_GLOW
global TEX_ANGLER_ICON
